          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Generalized Reedy model structures are a class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            that generalize the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structures"} Reedy model structures
            when the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            is generalized from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+category"} Reedy category
            to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Reedy+category"} generalized Reedy category
          %p
            So these model structures serve to present
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-categories of (∞,1)-functors
            on generalized Reedy categories.
          %p
            As for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structures
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+shapes+for+higher+structures"} geometric shapes for higher structures
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms"} automorphisms
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            be a (Berger-Moerdijk)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Reedy+category"} generalized Reedy category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a category with small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
          %h3#the_model_structure The model structure
          #FirstNotation.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in S
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : S \to \mathcal{C}
              and every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : X \to Y
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^+(s)
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^+/s
                  on the non-invertible morphisms into
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^-(s)
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/under+category"} under category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mo −
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s/S^-
                  on the non-invertible morphisms out of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %li
                %p write
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Latch
                          %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %munder
                            %mi lim
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi r
                                %mo →
                                %mi s
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∈
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mo +
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi s
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Latch_s(X) \coloneqq  {\lim_{\underset{(r \to s) \in S^+(s)}{\to}}} X(r)
                %p
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  over
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mo +
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^+(s)
                  %strong latching object
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  at
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %li
                %p write
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Match
                          %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %munder
                            %mi lim
                            %munder
                              %mo ←
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi s
                                %mo →
                                %mi r
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∈
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mo −
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi s
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Match_s(X) \coloneqq {\lim_{\underset{(s \to r) \in S^-(s)}{\leftarrow}}} X(r)
                %p
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  over
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mo −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^-(s)
                  %strong matching object
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  at
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %li
                %p write
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi s
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Latch
                              %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mi Latch
                          %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_s \coprod_{Latch_s(X)} Latch_s(Y) \to Y_s
                %p
                  for the universal morphism induced from the morphism
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_s(X) \to X_s
                  %strong relative latching map
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                  at
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %li
                %p write
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi s
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Match
                          %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mrow
