                                %mo −
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∈
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mo +
                          %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \stackrel{\in S^-}{\to} \stackrel{\in S^+}{\to} s
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d/i_s
                  is non-empty;
              %li
                %p
                  similarly, since every morphism factors essentially uniquely in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d / i_s
                  constructed from the isomorphisms that exhibit the essentially unique factorization.
            %p
              With this the statement follows from the fact that restriction along cofinal functors preserves colimits and the pointwise description of left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              over comma categories:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
